  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)=x^2+9, g(x)=\\frac{x}{x-9}$ and $\\mathrm{a}=f \\circ g(10), \\mathrm{b}=g \\circ f(3)$. If $\\mathrm{e}$ and $l$ denote the eccentricity and the length of the latus rectum of the ellipse $\\frac{x^2}{a}+\\frac{y^2}{b}=1$, then $8 \\mathrm{e}^2+l^2$ is equal to.",
    "image": null
  },
