  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & f(x)=x^2+9 \\quad g(x)=\\frac{x}{x-9} \\\\ & a=f(g(10))=f\\left(\\frac{10}{10-9}\\right) \\\\ & =f(10)=109 \\\\ & b=g(f(3))=g(9+9) \\\\ & =g(18)=\\frac{18}{9}=2 \\\\ & E: \\frac{x^2}{109}+\\frac{y^2}{2}=1\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{e}^2=1-\\frac{2}{109}=\\frac{107}{109} \\\\ & \\ell=\\frac{2(2)}{\\sqrt{109}}=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{109}} \\\\ & 8 \\mathrm{e}^2+\\ell^2=\\frac{8(107)}{109}+\\frac{16}{109} \\\\ & =8\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
